findings.fix:
Cancel the goal instead of doing nothing on an empty path — `setGoal(null)` clears `stateGoal` and the path via `resetPath('goal_updated')` without setting `stopPathing`, so it cannot latch:

```js
function stopOnce() {
  if (ctx.lastGoalKey !== 'idle') {
    if (bot.pathfinder.isMoving()) bot.pathfinder.stop()
    else bot.pathfinder.setGoal(null)
    ctx.lastGoalKey = 'idle'
  }
}
```

The new guard test (bot/test/tick.test.js:69-99) then needs its `calls.setGoal` expectation bumped, since the idle tick issues a `setGoal(null)`; `calls.effectiveGoals` and the no-latch assertion still hold. A ticker test that a parked dynamic follow goal is cleared by `ticker.stop()` would cover the regression directly.

